## Why This Is Asked
Assesses design for fair throughput, scalability, and auditable enforcement in a shared data lake.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant quotas; token bucket; API Gateway usage plans; DynamoDB; Lambda; S3 prefixes; CloudWatch; Kinesis Firehose; testing at scale.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst;
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test multi-tenant fairness under bursty conditions and validate SLA guarantees?
- What changes if large tenants typically spike during business hours?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-account access, tenant isolation, and end-to-end data export controls in a realistic setup.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account roles and STS AssumeRole with session tags
- S3 prefixes and object-level permissions
- TLS enforcement and per-tenant KMS keys
- CloudTrail auditing of cross-account activity

## Code Example

```json
// Trust policy for the tenant-scoped ExportRole
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::DATA-LAKE-ACCOUNT:role/ExporterRole" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": { "StringEquals": { "aws:RequestTag/tenant_id": "tenant-123" } }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
